Don't mention it.

144
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:08,280
All right, we're back so now let's take a look at three phrases we picked out on Fluency Builder.

145
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:08,510
Fluency Builder.

146
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:15,120
So, we have a great phrase here, something that we often hear in conversation, polite conversations.

147
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:17,020
The older man says, I'm in no hurry.

148
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:18,900
Now, what does this mean?

149
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:20,480
Does this mean he needs to go somewhere?

150
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,920
No, he says, you know what?

151
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:24,680
I really don't have to go anywhere fast.

152
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:29,260
That's why he let her, the girl, get in front of him in line at the shop.

153
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:31,540
All right, so basically it means I can wait.

154
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:32,480
I can wait, yeah.

155
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:34,720
So, if somebody says, oh, I'll be right back.

156
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:35,940
Please wait a moment.

157
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:37,800
You can say, I'm in no hurry.

158
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:38,740
Take your time.

159
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:43,520
Okay, so I'm in no hurry means it's not that important.

160
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,200
I don't have to go fast.

161
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:51,500
Right, but if you change the no and you say, I'm in a hurry, then that means that you have to go fast.

162
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:52,100
Come on, Marco.

163
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:53,120
Speed it up.

164
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:54,180
I'm in a hurry.

165
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:56,080
I'm in a hurry.

166
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,080
Okay.

167
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,080
Yes.

168
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:00,960
So, just changing those two words, that gives you a completely different meaning.

169
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:04,160
And well, the girl, Michelle, she said, oh, that's so nice of you.

170
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:04,720
Thank you very much.

171
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,280
And he says, my pleasure.

172
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:09,980
All right, so this is an alternative to the phrase, you're welcome.

173
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:12,780
This is a very polite way to say you're welcome.

174
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:19,380
And so, when we hear her thank him for something, you know, thank you for letting me go ahead of you, he says, my pleasure.

175
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:21,360
This is a great, great phrase for you guys.

176
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:21,920
Exactly.

177
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:28,340
So, now you have another alternative instead of saying, you're welcome or no problem or don't mention it.

178
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:30,810
Now you have, it's my pleasure.

179
00:08:31,130 --> 00:08:34,250
This is a little bit more formal, but you can use it in any circumstance.

180
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:34,950
That's right.

181
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:41,270
And as I said, another option here is the phrase, don't mention it, which means exactly the same thing.

182
00:08:41,530 --> 00:08:41,770
You're welcome.

183
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:42,250
That's right.

184
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,560
So, the older gentleman says, thanks for the suggestions.

185
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:46,210
Thanks for your help.

186
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,270
And what does the young woman say?

187
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:49,390
Don't mention it.

188
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:50,110
Don't mention it.

189
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:51,910
So, this is more colloquial.

190
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:54,130
This is a little bit more spoken language.

191
00:08:55,230 --> 00:08:56,410
She's saying, no problem.

192
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:57,840
You're welcome.

193
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:58,400
That's right.

194
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:03,700
So, you have, you're welcome, no problem, my pleasure, don't mention it.

195
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,720
All ways of saying the same thing.

196
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:06,840
All right.

197
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,840
So, let's take another listen to our dialogue.

198
